<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Larova · Spanish strings (European Spanish; es-419 is deferred, docs/localization.md §3).

  A translation, not a source: never fix wording here. Fix the English in values/strings.xml and
  re-translate, or the two drift apart. See docs/localization.md.

  **A model draft, not yet read by a native speaker.** docs/localization.md §5 names the three
  parts that must not ship on a machine draft — the help bar and contact sheet, the two view names,
  and the six templates — so those are where a review pass starts.

  Address form: impersonal wherever Spanish allows it; "tú" where an address form is unavoidable,
  which is what a phone in a family reads like. Typographic apostrophes (’) throughout.
-->
